  "result": "Perfect! All 38 tests pass (14 new tests for the two new functions). \n\n## Summary\n\nAdded two utility functions to `src/invoices.js`:\n\n**lineTotal(line)** \u2014 Calculates qty \u00d7 unitPrice for a single line\n- Validates that qty is a positive integer\n- Validates that unitPrice is a non-negative integer\n- Returns `ok(cents)` or `fail(ERROR_CODE)`\n\n**invoiceTotals(invoice)** \u2014 Calculates totals for an entire invoice\n- Validates invoice structure (must be object with non-empty lines array)\n- Sums line totals using lineTotal()\n- Returns `ok({ subtotal, total })` where subtotal = total (for now)\n- Uses roundCents() to ensure all money amounts stay as integer cents\n\n**Error codes added:**\n- LINE_INVALID: A line must have a positive quantity and a non-negative unit price.\n- INVOICE_INVALID: An invoice must be an object with a lines array.\n\n**Test coverage** \u2014 14 new tests covering calculation accuracy, validation, edge cases (zero prices, large numbers), non-mutation, and error handling.",
